'''tooth-blanch†''' (töth′blȧnch), ''n.'' Something to whiten the teeth; a dentifrice.

{{smaller block|''Dentifricium'', tooth-powder, tooth sope, or ''tooth-blanch''.
{{right|''Nomenclator'', 1585. (''Nares.'')}}}}

'''tooth-brush''' (töth′brush), ''n.'' A small brush, with a long straight or curved handle, used for cleaning the teeth.

'''toothbrush-tree''' (töth′brush-trē), ''n.'' See ''Salvadora''<sup>1</sup>.

'''tooth-carpenter''' (töth′kär″pẹn-tėr), ''n.'' A dentist. [Humorous slang.]

'''tooth-cress''' (töth′kres), ''n.'' Same as ''coralwort''.

'''tooth-drawer†''' (töth′drâ″ėr), ''n.'' [< ME. ''toth-drawer, tothdraware''; < ''tooth'' + ''drawer''.] One who draws teeth, especially as a profession; a dentist.

{{smaller block|Of portours and of pykeporses, and pyled [bald] ''toth-drawers.''
{{right|''Piers Plowman'' (C), vii. 370.}}}}

{{smaller block|His face so ill favouredly made that he looks at all times as if a ''toothdrawer'' were fumbling about his gums.
{{right|''Dekker'', Gull's Hornbook.}}}}

